{"seconds": 36.8, "exit": 0, "final": "After fxe6, Rxe6 wins a pawn but Black has checks. However, Nxe6+ without fxe6 (i.e., after Kg8 or Kh8) leads to Nxc7 winning the queen, which is much better. Let me verify the main line once more:\n\n**Best move: Nxe6+**\n\n**Main line:** \n1. Nxe6+ Kg8 (or Kh8)\n2. Nxc7 - White wins the queen\n\nThis is a **fork motif** \u2013 the knight checks the king and simultaneously attacks the undefended queen.\n\n**Coaching note:**\nWhen your opponent's pieces are undefended, look for checks that attack them simultaneously. Here, Nxe6+ forces the king to move while the queen on c7 remains hanging. After the king moves, Nxc7 wins the queen outright. Always scan for pieces that defend your target \u2013 this queen had no defenders.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nxe6+\", \"line\": [\"Nxe6+\", \"Kg8\", \"Nxc7\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RRK1 w - - 2 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RRK1 w - - 2 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RRK1 w - - 2 20", "square": "c7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RRK1 w - - 2 20", "square": "f8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RRK1 w - - 2 20", "square": "e7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RRK1 w - - 2 20", "square": "g7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RRK1 w - - 2 20", "square": "d2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RRK1 w - - 2 20", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r4r2/ppq1npkp/4p1p1/3p2N1/8/8/PPPQ2PP/4RR